%I A081082 #16 Oct 04 2026 15:15:34
%S A081082 2,0,2,1,4,5,14,31,84,258,856,3557,16912,102889,796480
%N A081082 Number of unlabeled, connected ortho-projection graphs on n vertices.
%C A081082 The number of all, not necessarily connected, unlabeled ortho-projection graphs on n vertices equals the number of inequivalent binary LCD codes of length n, where equivalence is by permutation of coordinates. This follows by associating a symmetric idempotent matrix P with the nondegenerate subspace Im(P). - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Oct 04 2026
%D A081082 B. Shtylla and L. Zulli, Ortho-projection graphs, in preparation.
%H A081082 M. Harada, <a href="https://www.math.is.tohoku.ac.jp/~mharada/LCD2/">Binary LCD codes</a> (Magma classification data).
%H A081082 M. Harada and Y. Tanaka, <a href="https://doi.org/10.3934/amc.2025034">On the classification of binary LCD codes</a>, Advances in Mathematics of Communications, 20 (2026), 136-150.
%H A081082 L. Zulli, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20120430091319/https://www.cs.lafayette.edu/~zullil/">Home Page</a>
%F A081082 Let b(n) be the number of inequivalent binary LCD codes of length n. Then 1 + Sum_{n>=1} b(n)*x^n = Product_{n>=1} (1 - x^n)^(-a(n)). Equivalently, a(n) is the inverse Euler transform of b(n). - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Oct 04 2026
%Y A081082 Cf. A081080, A081081.
%K A081082 nonn,hard,more,changed
%O A081082 1,1
%A A081082 B. Shtylla and L. Zulli (shtyllab(AT)lafayette.edu, zullil(AT)lafayette.edu), Mar 05 2003
%E A081082 a(9)-a(10) from _Sean A. Irvine_, Oct 09 2025
%E A081082 a(11)-a(15) from _Vladeta Jovovic_, Oct 04 2026
